      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be possible to use [aggregate initialization syntax](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/aggregate_initialization.html) to ensure that if fields are reordered/renamed/etc then we will remember to fix this up?  For example: `DecodingState fullImageDecodingState \u003d { .fDst \u003d decodingState.fPreblendBuffer, ... }`.\n\nI am also open to other alternatives where fields are named.  (I wondered about `DecodingState fullImageDecodingState \u003d *decodingState; fullImageDecodingState.fDst \u003d ...`, but the copy assignment would unnecessarily copy `fPreblendBuffer`.\n\nI also note that after my suggestions to fold/hoist `fFirstRow`, `fLastRow`, etc into `DecodingState` the struct will get quite big.  So maybe now would be a good time to extract a smaller `DecodingDst` struct with just the things you have here (`fDst`, `fDstRowStride`, `fDstRowSize`, `fDstBytesPerPixel`)?  That way here the smaller `fullImageDecodingDst` could be used instead of the bigger `fullImageDecodingState`.\n\nWDYT?",
